speechtext:
Madam Speaker, 1 rise under Standing Order 43. In view of the takeover by the CDIC of Crown corporations and ailing private-sector companies, which was announced yesterday, to be led by the men who gave us the Canadian ownership charge of 4.5 cents per gallon imposed to permit Petro-Canada to purchase Petrofina
Oral Questions
from the Belgians, now to save Dome from itself, and next to float the sinking subsidiaries of CDIC, I move, seconded by the Hon. Member for Simcoe North (Mr. Lewis):
That this House conclude that
With Austin, Strong and Bell
The public sector is going to hell;
With deals that startle by smell
The country is clearly not well;
Canadians now toil for Joel Bell,
Their land is Strong's-it's time to rebel.

On the Order: Government Notices of Motions:
November 23, 1982-The President of the Privy Council:
That, commencing at 5.59 o'clock p.m., on Wednesday, December 22, 1982, or, as the case may be, at the time that the House concludes its consideration of Government Business on that day, the temporary changes to the Standing Orders set forward as Appendix C of the Third Report of the Special Committee on Standing Orders and Procedure, tabled Friday, November 5, 1982, shall take effect;
That the proposed changes in the Standing Orders shall be applied in the spirit expressed in Part II (entitled "Recommended Experimental Changes") of the Third Report of the Special Committee on Standing Orders and Procedure;
That, subject to future Order of the House, the said temporary changes to the Standing Orders shall cease to have effect at 5.59 o'clock p.m., on Wednesday,
